<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Marseille defeat RC Lens as they win five in a row in Ligue 1</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:454a3775b3760525f39c1d9477c0580760f4f31e1f633b5c2a085ab57a4dd767</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T06:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261109-marseille-defeat-rc-lens-as-they-win-five-in-a-row-in-ligue-1--be4258802e9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261109-marseille-defeat-rc-lens-as-they-win-five-in-a-row-in-ligue-1" /><summary type="html">Marseille beat Lens (2-1) in the final game of Ligue 1 matchday 10. Thanks to this result, OM are 4th in the table.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Europe to press US on Ukraine peace and Iran at Paris G7 talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28143dfdeebf6c895190d375f245df15457eea9f609afdb29cb42d7cc9b732cd</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T02:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-europa-us-ukraine-peace-iran-paris-g7-ministers--6e388c018d93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-europa-us-ukraine-peace-iran-paris-g7-ministers" /><summary type="html">G7 foreign ministers will revisit Russia’s war in Ukraine and the prospect of further US strikes on Iran when they meet in Paris on Monday. Washington has kept the option of new strikes open since Republicans lost the midterm elections. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is due to attend both days, unlike the March meeting where he only came for one.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Trump vows comeback as parties clash over Democrat prosecution threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:315f92db0737a4b61d9d49f7091dc6ccc25c9057a61e15f3a09b37e1292b42ae</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T01:13:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261109-trump-comeback-democrats-prosecution-threats--3ddd0d742c90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261109-trump-comeback-democrats-prosecution-threats" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump vowed a political comeback on Sunday after Republicans lost control of Congress in last Tuesday’s midterms, as incoming Democratic leaders pledged to hold his administration to account, and the attorney general promised to defend officials against threatened prosecutions.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia to probe reports that Chinese intelligence targeted CEO Jensen Huang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0ffbf4abe20cd9ad148431b9a37fb36abd599ab1f83bfa77f2a45255a17c70b</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T23:02:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20261108-nvidia-jensen-huang-chinese-intelligence-probe--cbcae134d3b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261108-nvidia-jensen-huang-chinese-intelligence-probe" /><summary type="html">Nvidia’s board said Sunday it would investigate reports that CEO Jensen Huang was targeted by a foreign intelligence operation. The New York Times reported Huang had an affair with an executive US intelligence believed was gathering information for Beijing. Huang will remain CEO during the inquiry and has pledged cooperation.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo criticises Milei’s austerity in Argentina, says growth must benefit all</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4c65417e7ff0575230c87925846d8dc216747212d05da49454fde428f83d842</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T22:23:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-argentina-visit-milei--0e21f75a1391.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-argentina-visit-milei" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV arrived in Argentina on Sunday from Uruguay, where his Latin America tour began, facing calls to help bridge divisions after three years of austerity under President Javier Milei. The visit to Buenos Aires is the first by a pontiff to the late Pope Francis’s homeland in nearly four decades.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal Politics and Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a339748a9fa780172bcd0885da0cdfe49c1fd9d792dbd3b58b0e1f2440847cd</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T21:16:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261108-pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru--dde1c7121fce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261108-pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his Papacy so far. The pontiff has wrapped up his first visit to Uruguay. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and the co-host of the 'Inside the Vatican' podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of his Latin American tour.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot begins the hard work of forging a coalition government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d680f3569b4bc281e3b9b0c82a7e06c6ecb89b44b4b7aa6026321f52fb2754c7</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T21:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government--f27d5923499e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot was tapped by President Isaac Herzog to try to form a government Sunday evening. But his lack of a clear majority in parliament will make trying to forge a coalition alongside the country's divided minor parties an uphill struggle.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal Politics and Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d66f3bbb9998582dedc93a3ac51da36b10894c4e00aa65e5c7d487dc5351c05</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T20:51:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru--8b6e4f16329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his Papacy so far. The pontiff has wrapped up his first visit to Uruguay. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and the co-host of the 'Inside the Vatican' podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of his Latin America trip.</summary></entry><entry><title>Migrant boat sinks off Senegal, killing at least 34 people, authorities say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:840ee2e0fcf01dd8fac0a8f95debaac2c6cd8be8581084ffae63a90cc2989588</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:55:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T20:40:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say--c7e270d5fde4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say" /><summary type="html">A boat carrying migrants along the hazardous Atlantic Ocean route from West Africa to Europe sank off the coast of Senegal, killed at least 34 people, authorities said Sunday. Only one survivor has so far been found, and "an indeterminate number" are still missing.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russian strikes leave hundreds of thousands without power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e2d4a896951ccbe9fa391c3f82b1fcd676f1bc9afee041b0acb2365db3bc1ea</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:59:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-russian-strikes-leave-hundreds-of-thousands-without-power--c719f8373e32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-russian-strikes-leave-hundreds-of-thousands-without-power" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of Ukrainians were left without electricity on Sunday following Russian airstrikes targeting the country's energy infrastructure. Moscow has intensified its attacks as winter approaches, leaving residents in Kyiv and other parts of the country struggling with power cuts as temperatures continue to drop. Clemence Waller reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22fed43f8c059597cbd227b693ab2ea1ffac3e3ab987115a055936d4a26f411c</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:58:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government--3797dae49af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's Alcaraz beats error-prone Shelton to win Paris Masters for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da95486014e0455e310d6ed86c3a8b30f173a5ae7defd2837c89cfa5af788071</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:31:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261108-spain-s-alcaraz-beats-error-prone-shelton-to-win-paris-masters-for-first-time--26fab0b94fb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261108-spain-s-alcaraz-beats-error-prone-shelton-to-win-paris-masters-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">Spanish tennis star Carlos Alcaraz avenged his loss to American player Ben Shelton in the US Open in September as he inched ahead of his rival Sunday to win the Paris Masters for the first time. It was Shelton's first defeat in a Masters final.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: US midterms 'Blue Wave', French protests and Dakar Youth Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:339852d6d26d7bc7145a46d34756b03316f6cf94c8f519f25e60ad6fd0856a67</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:21:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics--c8336674c1f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics" /><summary type="html">From the Democratic Party's big wins in the US midterm elections to France's ongoing student-led protests and the first Olympic sports event held on African soil, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US voters reject AI data centres: could the backlash spread to France?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:924e4183f3c8ace7dad5dba25715b92677272789b59420e1845627097bd6a097</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:36:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261108-us-voters-reject-ai-data-centres-could-the-backlash-spread-to-france--b2902e041847.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261108-us-voters-reject-ai-data-centres-could-the-backlash-spread-to-france" /><summary type="html">In Tuesday’s US midterm elections, voters weighed in on more than 40 local measures on data centres, and sided against them in all but one. With Democrats taking control of Congress in January and new governors in Texas and Georgia calling for moratoriums, the AI building boom faces its toughest political test yet.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1be47f1ad539715d8f191e8f376beba37afece7fcb234655ba67aea7eca3d69</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:22:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens--95e6e91a4caa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens" /><summary type="html">One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9def451b916fa04be63884306faa1a287bae0950e09bb43bf06622b9d21d0ab7</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:21:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting--b5967a40cc64.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. FRANCE 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.</summary></entry><entry><title>French skipper wins Route du Rhum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75bcedf2288d3d9eff1231b3100be2137e5b8520e7e5eec9e065b14091029724</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:20:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-skipper-wins-route-du-rhum--51e11d53f461.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-skipper-wins-route-du-rhum" /><summary type="html">French sailor Tom Laperche has won the Route du Rhum, setting a new record in the transatlantic yacht race. The 29-year-old crossed the finish line in Guadeloupe on his first attempt, beating the previous 2022 record by around six hours. A remarkable debut in one of sailing's toughest competitions!</summary></entry><entry><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:012653e26d29cad1044deddd9c66ba225224ecfb6ba5b9fa16afc809d34cb014</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:18:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting--bd87f2f4ae08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66158b08fad72cc5b411b47c05953a804d7cfb1bc34325ba40a0644a5060ff17</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:16:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says--c38c48e4c7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says" /><summary type="html">France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo urges men to respect wives amid Latin American femicide crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b27690b467e2c2ffe5fd31c3b9acfa9391f417bbc4bf448d6e029b00ccae229</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:15:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america--c0353931a5d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV urged men to respect their wives as he wrapped up the first leg of his 12-day tour of Latin America. The region recorded nearly 20,000 instances of women being killed over the past five years alone, most of them murdered by a current or former partner.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘10 times more painful’: Menstrual disorders fuel calls to ban tear gas at French protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e3289264df00b7f95cabe8bce56f238f3614d25fd8e68aa2de49a668052dc67</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T11:53:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261108-abnormal-menstraution-periods-fuel-calls-ban-tear-gas-french-protests-police--8bbcd54e5ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261108-abnormal-menstraution-periods-fuel-calls-ban-tear-gas-french-protests-police" /><summary type="html">French police have made extensive use of tear gas during protests that have roiled France in recent weeks, sometimes causing grievous injuries. Thousands of accounts of women experiencing acutely painful periods and increased bleeding are further challenging assumptions that the chemical irritant carries only minor consequences.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Dakar Youth Olympic Games: Golden Double for Senegal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9b661315071af3d951b55bb6a79e2702f3b8a18a367f6bc7e61b2f9980672bd</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:56:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261108-2026-dakar-youth-olympic-games-golden-double-for-senegal--9648adca27a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261108-2026-dakar-youth-olympic-games-golden-double-for-senegal" /><summary type="html">Senegal won two gold medals in beach wrestling at the Youth Olympic Games in Dakar. Elisabeth Diatta won gold in the -55 kg category, the host country’s first gold medal at the Youth Olympic Games. Her compatriot Maguette Diop followed suit, taking gold in the -80 kg category.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Diwali: Over one billion people mark victory of light over darkness</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78dca016f5e110db402f37595c949fd0da16b6f98162753ccd7c126d18e9ebce</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:46:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness--093adc3e4b15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness" /><summary type="html">Diwali celebrations began on Sunday, with people across India and the global diaspora gathering to mark one of the most important festivals in the Hindu tradition. In Ayodhya, believed to be the birthplace of Lord Rama, the deity celebrated during the festival, festivities included performances based on the Hindu epic Ramayana, laser and light shows, live music, fireworks and drone displays.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguay: Senate impeached Peña rather than accept his offer to resign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f92e77a1652a3613ceb4e38210955996a47ec64ebc7bfafcf291780eeade858d</id><updated>2026-11-09T06:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe_a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign--268a291e27fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe%C3%B1a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign" /><summary type="html">Paraguay's ousted president, Santiago Peña, has been charged over the collapse of Ueno Bank. Initially placed under house arrest, he has since been transferred to a military facility for his own safety. Nearly three million customers were locked out of their accounts after regulators seized control of the online bank. Repayments are now under way, but protests continue as customers demand access to their money. Peña denies any wrongdoing. Jack Pownall reports.</summary></entry></feed>
